infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Memory-level parallelism: dependency structure sets the latency
  desc Same misses, same CPU — pointer-chains serialize them, independent loads overlap them
  compares
    - label Dependent loads — pointer chase
      children
        - label Each load waits for the previous result
          desc next = node.next, so the address lives inside the value you must load first
        - label N misses serialize into N times the miss latency
          desc Round-trips stack end to end with no overlap
        - label MLP unused — only 1 miss in flight
          desc Linked lists, trees, graphs all hit this wall
        - label Fix: contiguous arena plus software prefetch
          desc Restructure access order so the next address is known early
    - label Independent loads — index array
      children
        - label All addresses known up front
          desc arr[0], arr[1000], arr[2000], arr[3000] issue together
        - label N misses overlap into about one miss latency
          desc One round-trip plus small dispatch overhead, not N of them
        - label MLP exploited — 8–16 misses in flight
          desc The load buffer queues independent misses concurrently
        - label CSR adjacency with index-based access
          desc Future indices prefetch while current data is processed
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
